.TH CHIMPD 1 "2026-11" "chimp 0.6.0"
.SH NAME
chimpd \- Chimp's desktop service: MIDI controls to desktop actions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chimpd
.RB [ \-\-no\-tray ]
.br
.B chimpd
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B chimpd
listens to every MIDI controller on the ALSA sequencer and carries out the
actions set in
.BR chimp (1):
volume, mute, brightness, media keys, shortcuts, apps, commands and OBS
scenes. It shows the result in Plasma's on-screen display or its own
overlay, keeps the LPD8 mk2's pad lights in step with the desktop, and puts
an icon in the system tray.
.PP
It is meant to run as the systemd user service:
.PP
.RS
systemctl \-\-user enable \-\-now chimp.service
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-no\-tray
Run without the tray icon.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/chimp/
Settings, written by
.BR chimp (1);
changes are picked up while running.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/chimp.json
Current state, for the editor.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR chimp (1)
